// MQ-9 Reaper tail surfaces (V-tail and ventral fin) - lift and drag per
// surface area. Illustrative, derived from the Reaper's shape with standard
// aerodynamics, NOT official data:
// - a symmetric airfoil (roughly NACA 0012): CL 0 at 0 deg, the same both
//   ways;
// - short, stubby surfaces (aspect ratio ~4-5): 3D lift slope ~0.07/deg;
// - stalls at ~14 deg (CL ~1.0), dropping off after;
// - drag: profile 0.008 + induced 0.06 CL^2, plus a separation rise
//   through the stall, turning into flat-plate drag (1.25 sin^2 alpha);
// - covers -90..90 deg (the F-16 tail table it replaces stopped at +-15 and
//   held its edge values beyond - wrong for a fin in a big sideslip).
// Evenly spaced at 1 deg. Regenerate rather than hand-edit.
